# Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the project root to override defaults.

## Backend Configuration

```bash
# API Server
API_HOST=0.0.0.0
API_PORT=8000
API_RELOAD=true

# Database
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///data/papermill.db
# For PostgreSQL:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/papermill

# Frontend (for CORS)
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Logging
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Options: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL
```

## Frontend Configuration

Create `frontend/.env.local`:

```bash
# API Endpoint
REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api

# Build mode
REACT_APP_ENV=development
# Options: development, production
```

## Example `.env` Files

### Development

```bash
# .env (development)
API_HOST=0.0.0.0
API_PORT=8000
API_RELOAD=true
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///data/papermill.db
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
```

### Production

```bash
# .env (production)
API_HOST=0.0.0.0
API_PORT=80
API_RELOAD=false
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://prod_user:secure_password@db.example.com:5432/papermill
FRONTEND_URL=https://papermill.example.com
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
```
